SkeletonToast retains all trademark and patent rights to the Silver Star code.

This license shall be included in all copies or substantial portions of this project.

Permitted Uses:
1) Any part of the Silver Star project may be used, unconditionally, in personal, single-player settings. This includes unlimited modification to the codebase.
  1a) This clause DOES NOT allow unconditional redistribution of modified Silver Star projects.
2) Any part of the Silver Star project can be modified and used in ANY capacity, as long as the modified code is not redistributed.
  2a) This means that no permission or special rights are necessary if this code is modified or incorporated into a larger project that is NOT being redistributed. This includes usage in multiplayer settings.
3) Silver Star projects can be freely added to modpacks, datapack collections, and any other collections, as long as they remain unedited.

Prohibited Uses:
4) Code from any Silver Star project MAY NOT be used as part of any directly monetized project.
  4a) Any project including Silver Star code must be offered, with no charge, to the general public, and all users must be afforded the same permissions as outlined above (clauses 1-3).
5) Code from Silver Star projects may not be reused as part of a separate, publicly-released project.
  5a) Code may still be freely reused and modified in personal settings.
  5b) This exclusively refers to lifting code from a Silver Star project's codebase and repurposing it within another codebase.
  5c) See "Exemptions" for how this relates to the Silver Star Library project.

Usage Requirements:
6) If Silver Star code is included as part of a separate project, the same permissive rights as outlined above (clauses 1-3) must be granted to users of the separate project.
  6a) Inclusion of Silver Star code does not inherently grant SkeletonToast or the Silver Star team any rights or authority over the project at large, but rights are retained in regards to the Silver Star code.

Exemptions:
7) A special exemption is provided for the Silver Star Library project. This project may be modified, used, and redistributed in any capacity, provided clauses 4 and 6 are adhered to.
  7a) If a standalone, modified version of the Silver Star Library is redistributed, it must include a clear, upfront link to the original Silver Star Library project page.
8) SkeletonToast and the Silver Star team reserve the right to prohibit any individual, group, server, or any other entity from using Silver Star code in a public setting. This is at the SOLE DISCRETION of SkeletonToast and the Silver Star team.
  8a) The right to use Silver Star projects in personal or private settings is granted, provided all conditions of this License are followed, to all individuals.
9) SkeletonToast and the Silver Star team reserve the right to override any parts of this License, or introduce additional usage requirements, on an individual basis. Should this right be exercised by SkeletonToast or the Silver Star team, affected parties will be notified.
